Assumption challenge ledger
  Runner vertices preserve exact speed identity but destroy endpoint/component adjacency.
  q-obligation vertices preserve THM-523 covering necessity but destroy timing and binders.
  Parked-runner private obligations preserve the small-m resonance source but miss
    multi-parked rows where deletion leaves a covering core.
  Safe arcs/endpoints preserve constructive witnesses (THM-526) but W(A) is non-uniform.
  Binding-pair vertices preserve the exact LRC predicate (THM-524) but the crossing
    index j>=D/14 is tautological unless j is derived from non-M arithmetic.
  In this sample, arc residuals with no parked private obligation: 0/9

Hypothesis generated:
  HYP-2579 (proposed): after THM-523/524/526, the remaining proof is a
  private-obligation recursion.  Arc-width discharges large parked runners;
  principal towers collapse to k=1; the real residual consists of rows where
  deleting any parked runner either leaves another q-covering core or gives
  a small-m binding crossing whose private q-obligations determine the flank.
  The immediate correction is that q-covering and unit-residue coverage are
  different floors: {1..12,182} is a q-covering principal row with M=14/183,
  closer to 1/14 than the older {1..11,13,84} cover-all-unit champion.
